trategy.\n\nReason: (F, 3) is the best choice because it strengthens my central position and maintains "tempo" by making a quiet move that limits the opponent\'s options. Unlike (H, 4), it does not flip a large number of pieces that the opponent could immediately use as a bridge to play back into the center or edges. It blocks the opponent from taking F3 and builds a strong, stable group of pieces.\n\nAnswer: (F, 3)'}
