ty.\n4.  **Center moves (C6, D6, E6)**: These are acceptable "quiet" moves that fill holes, but they do not offer the same strategic stability as securing the edge with A7.\n\nReason: (A, 7) is the best move because it secures a long stable edge (A1-A7) without giving the opponent access to the corner A8. It also flips several interior opponent pieces, reducing their influence in the center and restricting their mobility, while leaving me with a solid position.\n\nAnswer: (A, 7)'}
